+\subsection{July 2026 Inference Optimization and Model Selection}
+
+A July~2026 optimization pass applied three changes --- batched sentence
+translation (replacing a one-sentence-per-call loop for HF-backed models),
+SDPA attention with a per-architecture eager/SDPA fallback (T5-based MADLAD
+rejects SDPA in transformers~5.4.0; Gemma3-based MiLMMT accepts it), and
+length-sorted batching with order restoration --- each validated against a
+$\pm$0.3 BLEU-parity gate. Translate-only throughput (measured separately from
+model load time, after a conflation bug in the original benchmark harness was
+found and fixed) rose 5.4$\times$ for NLLB-600M (383$\to$2{,}072\,chars/s),
+4.9$\times$ for MiLMMT-46-1B (74$\to$366\,chars/s), and 4.3$\times$ for
+Seamless-medium (73$\to$317\,chars/s).
+
+Two additional 2026 models were evaluated under the same 90-sentence
+FLORES-200 protocol and an 8\,GB VRAM budget, and rejected: NiuTrans
+LMT-60-1.7B (63.8 BLEU / 78.3 chrF, 6.6\,GB VRAM, 86\,chars/s) loses to the
+already-deployed MiLMMT-46-1B (65.2 BLEU, 3.4\,GB, 401\,chars/s) on every
+axis; a 5-sentence smoke test of LMT-60 had scored 73.2 BLEU, a reminder
+that small-sample BLEU is too noisy to drive a model-selection decision.
+Tencent Hunyuan-MT-7B, deployed as a 4-bit GGUF quantization (Q4\_K\_M) via
+Ollama, scored 54.7 BLEU --- below even NLLB-600M (55.3) and more than 12
+points under its published full-precision (bf16, WMT25-winning) reputation,
+indicating that on an 8\,GB budget, quantization loss can dominate a larger
+model's raw capacity. Table~\ref{tab:bleu} and Table~\ref{tab:compute}
+report both rejected candidates alongside the deployed models for
+transparency.
+
